from construct18 import R,read,save
p=read(R/'configs/prompts18_reference.json')['common']
p+='''
Framework-only abilities: the explicit state and candidate work are program-maintained. Return your JSON next action as above, or use a native retail tool call when needed. Actual parameters must be concrete, never a reference or placeholder. For prepare/confirm/submit copy default_arguments or current_goal IDs into the full required arguments schema. For clarify choose an actual different existing variant from related evidence; a missing catalogue is NOT evidence of nonexistence. The candidate list and preconditions are unchanged by context summarization.
evidence parameters={"refs":[integer reference IDs]} retrieves relevant stored raw records for the NEXT request only. Original history/catalogue/approvals remain in program storage. Do not request the whole history unnecessarily. You may call any of the native retail tools available in the request; exchange submission still goes through framework checks.
After a successful write choose stop; after withdrawal acknowledge and stop without a write. Do not treat a previous grant of specification permission as approval of a new complete plan. If user does not approve, continue resolving what is missing rather than claiming authorization. The shared controlled user judges the ACTUAL clarification or full proposal, and can accept or request correction. Neither a template nor a fingerprint counts as user approval by itself.
A formally observed stock result remains usable; a repeat query is an optional strategy, not a prerequisite to clarification. Review completed work feedback before repeating an identical query. When using compact state, current_goal plus default_arguments are the sole current operation targets; historical records in storage are not extra prerequisites. Missing preconditions indicate actual checks. related_variants are a limited cached subset, not the complete catalogue; evidence or a native query can resolve omitted information.'''
save(R/'configs/prompts19.json',{'framework':p,'official':'Unmodified tau2.agent.llm_agent.LLMAgent.system_prompt + official retail policy. No project instruction or helper tools inserted.','user_extractor_source':'src/user19.py EXTRACT; semantic extraction is simulator overhead, not Agent tokens.'})
save(R/'configs/budget.json',{'model':'deepseek-flash','temperature':0,'thinking':False,'timeout_seconds':60,'agent_request_attempt_limit':24,'agent_turn_limit':12,'agent_returned_tokens_soft_limit':60000,'executed_operation_limit':9,'max_response_tokens':1300,'sdk_and_application_retries':0,'simulator_semantic_requests_per_trajectory':12,'simulator_max_response_tokens':850,'simulator_tokens':'separate; not charged to Agent budget','official_terminal':'actual write then natural acknowledgment, or valid withdrawal acknowledgment','context_diagnostic_terminal':'stop on actual write, identical in original and compact branches'})
save(R/'configs/official_integration.json',{'unchanged':['LLMAgent.get_init_state','LLMAgent.generate_next_message','llm_utils.generate','official system instructions and domain policy','native RetailTools schemas and use_tool execution'],'in_memory_transport_hook':'llm_utils.completion -> same DeepSeek OpenAI SDK endpoint. No agent selection or conversation logic replaced. get_response_cost disabled: alias pricing unknown; raw usage and cache retained.','baseline_no_project_gate':True,'simulator':'LLM extracts only actual assistant text with exact quotes; program validates scope/specification/stock/amount/payment before user approves. Approval list is evaluation/simulator-side only; does not intercept official tools.','data':'18th-round controlled adaptations; original benchmark private instructions/reference actions remain archived and never enter Agent.'})
